# Conformance tests that legitimately stay on the print/println BUILTIN, exempt
# from conformance-builtin-print.sh. One conformance-relative path per line.
# Keep this list SMALL — each entry needs a reason.

# Tests of the print/println BUILTIN's own behavior — converting them to
# testing.Println would defeat their purpose (the builtin still exists).
conformance/101_println_managed_chars.bn
conformance/287_float_println.bn
conformance/317_native_println_int.bn
conformance/428_uint_print.bn
# Rejects spreading `m...` into the builtin (which has no variadic param);
# testing.Println IS user-variadic, so it cannot express this negative test.
conformance/spec/10-functions/181_err_spread_builtin.bn

# Temporary — a nil managed-pointer field deref (`p.val`, p == nil) does not
# raise the VM's --check-nil fault when boxed into testing.Println's ...*any
# (the box takes the field address, not a load through nil p). Distinct from the
# named-pointer-deref boxing case, which was fixed (see claude-todo any-boxing
# entry). Convert once that remaining case is fixed.
conformance/1142_nil_pointer_deref.bn
